WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Twice a year, Muslims everywhere put on
their best clothes and pray in mosques,

2
00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.960
halls and parks.

3
00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.940
The first comes when a
month of fasting ends.

4
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.280
It starts with thanks and something sweet,

5
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.800
such as dates.

6
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.250
The second falls during the Hajj.

7
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:22.450
After the prayer, a sheep, goat, cow
or camel is sacrificed in Allah's name.

8
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.190
So why is one of these two great
festivals marked by a sacrifice?

9
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.660
In this mission, you'll read a Qur'an
passage that calls an old story a clear

10
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:32.790
test.

11
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.920
Then you'll see how Muslims celebrate,
from the festival prayer to the family

12
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:37.950
meal.

13
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.980
Your mission: find out why one of these
festivals is marked by a sacrifice.
